// isolate-docs.birnam — reference-only registrations for I1b/L2 isolate APIs.
// Kept outside isolate.birnam so prose changes cannot alter executable image
// replay streams or the portable replacement-policy method operations.

[Doc module: #isolate is: "Blocking process isolates, health-checked single-worker replacement, and mailbox-safe worker-local live rollout."];

[Doc for: #start:selector:image: in: #isolate says:
  "Start one worker process from an explicit full-image baseline. Resolve receiver and one-argument selector inside that image, wait for ready, and answer an opaque ready handle or IsolateFailure."];
[Doc for: #start:selector:image:timeout: in: #isolate says:
  "As start:selector:image:, with an explicit nonnegative ready deadline in milliseconds."];
[Doc for: #request: in: #isolate says:
  "On an Isolate handle, send one copied value and block for its copied reply using the default deadline. The handle is single-flight."];
[Doc for: #request:timeout: in: #isolate says:
  "On an Isolate handle, send one copied value with an explicit millisecond deadline. Application errors leave the worker ready; uncertain post-send timeout, transport, protocol, or exit outcomes are terminal."];
[Doc for: #stop in: #isolate says:
  "Stop and reap an idle worker. Repeated stop after a recorded reap is idempotent; an exhausted reap budget reports #reapPending for later host-boundary drain."];
[Doc for: #stopWithTimeout: in: #isolate says:
  "Stop an idle worker with an explicit stop-acknowledgement deadline before bounded close, TERM, KILL, and reap escalation."];
[Doc for: #state in: #isolate says:
  "The process-local handle state: #starting, #ready, #busy, #stopping, #reapPending, or #exited."];

[Doc for: #replace:using: in: #isolate says:
  "Replace selected idle worker A with a healthy B between calls. The spec Map supplies #receiver, #selector, #image, #healthRequest, #readyTimeout, #healthTimeout, and #stopTimeout. Every B startup/health failure retains usable A; success selects B and reaps A, or reports B selected with A as the sole pending cleanup owner."];
[Doc for: #status in: #isolate says:
  "On IsolateReplacement, #failed, #replaced, or #cleanupPending."];
[Doc for: #currentWorker in: #isolate says:
  "On IsolateReplacement, the selected usable handle after the attempt: A before selection failure, B after successful health selection."];
[Doc for: #priorWorker in: #isolate says:
  "On IsolateReplacement, the worker selected before the attempt."];
[Doc for: #pendingCleanup in: #isolate says:
  "On IsolateReplacement, the sole process-local handle awaiting reap, or nil."];
[Doc for: #failure in: #isolate says:
  "On IsolateReplacement, the structured IsolateFailure which caused failure or partial cleanup, or nil."];

[Doc for: #evolve:timeout: in: #isolate says:
  "On an idle worker handle, send one fixed copied activate/rollback control and block. The worker compares its own digest, prepares and commits only between application calls under native quiescence, and answers EvolutionReceipt or a distinguishable transport/protocol IsolateFailure. There is no retry or fan-out."];
[Doc for: #operation in: #isolate says:
  "On EvolutionReceipt, #activate or #rollback."];
[Doc for: #module in: #isolate says:
  "On EvolutionReceipt, the activated module Symbol, or nil for rollback."];
[Doc for: #acceptedBaseDigest in: #isolate says:
  "On EvolutionReceipt, the lowercase SHA-256 base digest accepted for comparison by the worker."];
[Doc for: #priorDigest in: #isolate says:
  "On EvolutionReceipt, the worker generation digest before this control."];
[Doc for: #currentDigest in: #isolate says:
  "On EvolutionReceipt, the worker generation digest after acceptance or rejection."];
[Doc for: #outcome in: #isolate says:
  "On EvolutionReceipt, #activated, #rolledBack, or #rejected."];
[Doc for: #errorKind in: #isolate says:
  "On a rejected EvolutionReceipt, the kinded worker-local policy/mechanism reason; nil on success."];
[Doc for: #message in: #isolate says:
  "The diagnostic message on IsolateFailure, IsolateReplacement, or EvolutionReceipt."];
[Doc for: #class in: #isolate says:
  "On IsolateFailure, the structural failure class: #boot, #application, #protocol, #encode, #timeout, #transport, #exit, #busy, or #stopped."];
[Doc for: #kind in: #isolate says:
  "On IsolateFailure or IsolateReplacement, the kinded local or remote reason."];
[Doc for: #exitStatus in: #isolate says:
  "On IsolateFailure, the recorded child exit status when known, otherwise nil."];
[Doc for: #requestId in: #isolate says:
  "On IsolateFailure, the wire request id when transmission allocated one, otherwise nil."];
[Doc for: #isError in: #isolate says:
  "True for IsolateFailure, failed IsolateReplacement, and rejected EvolutionReceipt; false for successful or cleanup-pending replacement results and accepted receipts."];
[Doc for: #apiVersion in: #isolate says:
  "The implemented isolate workflow level, currently #I1b on Isolate; live rollout is #L2 through evolve:timeout:."]
